  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes between the lotteries and prefer the one with the more favorable (i.e., higher) sum. In this case, the only non-zero pairwise difference is between -3000 and -6000, which is 3000. The sum of pairwise differences is 3000, and it is the same regardless of which lottery is labeled. Therefore, the sum is equal for both lotteries — the reason would lead to indifference. However, the individual does not mention this sum or any calculation involving differences in outcomes. Instead, they focus entirely on the probability of not losing anything (i.e., getting 0 euros), which is a different consideration. The individual’s justification is based on a different criterion — risk of loss avoidance — not on the sum of outcome differences. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual did not consider or reference the sum of pairwise outcome differences at all. The reasoning process described is entirely inconsistent with the decision reason's structure and content.",
